    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) passes and the build is green.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` fields are unified into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` \u2014 e.g. the run produced `NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, fiscal year `27`, hash `16E6609E`, Luhn check `1`).\n\n**Files touched (7):**\n- **`MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: region from `Locality`, 2-digit `FiscalYear`, the same upper-hex 8-char `SHA-256(telephone+lastName)` as the old region-and-hash identity, and a Luhn `CHK` (reusing the existing `CheckDigit` helper) over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Carries the collision handling (`deduplicate`) and a `regionOf` that reads the leading region letters.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed the persisted accessor to `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`; removed the derived `getMembershipNumber`/`getCheckDigit`. Kept the DB column `customer_code` so no schema files were touched.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `addOwner` now calls `MemberId.of(...)`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` derive the region via `MemberId.regionOf(owner.getMemberId())`.\n- **`OwnerAuditListener.java`** \u2014 the human and structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit records reference `memberId`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the three DTO properties with a single `memberId`.\n- Deleted **`CustomerCode.java`** (its `deduplicate` referenced the removed getter).\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n\nEach edited method stayed CC-1 (rename accessors, one-line controller/mapper swaps), so the costly high-`WMC_other` classes (`Owner`, the controller) each absorbed only trivial single-line changes. New behaviour landed as one small, self-contained class (`MemberId`) rather than growing `Owner`, and I reused the existing `CheckDigit` Luhn helper instead of duplicating it. I avoided touching the DB schema/data files (kept the `customer_code` column) to hold the file-count multiplier down \u2014 the deleted `CustomerCode.java` was the only removal forced by compilation.\n\nOne note: `MembershipNumber.java` is now unused but still compiles; I left it in place rather than expand the change set, since deleting it would only add to the files-touched multiplier without any functional benefit. Say the word if you'd prefer it removed for cleanliness.",
